From: shirogane <artoriapendragon123@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] video: sunxi: add the srgn_splash boot logo command for the D1s

srgn_splash retains scanout until the Linux DRM modules take over near
APP startup. D1 mixer and DSI drivers stop inherited DMA and reset the
shared host state at takeover. Explicit cleanup remains on reinitialization
and error paths. The /chosen bus has identity address translation so
simpledrm can acquire and later release the framebuffer reservation.

Panel parameters live in the merged control FDT (srgn,panel-timing,
srgn,dsi-lanes, srgn,init-sequence, plus the reset-gpios and backlight pwms
the tree already carries), so a different screen stays a device tree overlay
and a logo image, not a U-Boot rebuild.

Register sequences follow the mainline Linux drivers (sun8i_mixer,
sun4i_tcon, sun6i_mipi_dsi, phy-sun6i-mipi-dphy, ccu-sun20i-d1) rather than
the Allwinner BSP. The clocking keeps the TCON and the D-PHY in exact
agreement by deriving both from the same 24 MHz maths: PLL_VIDEO0 runs at
4x the per-lane bit rate so its /4 tap feeds tcon-lcd0 directly, and the
D-PHY's own PLL is programmed to the identical rate.
---
diff --git a/drivers/Makefile b/drivers/Makefile
index 43d0ba33..dcac1d4b 100644
--- a/drivers/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/Makefile
@@ -46,6 +46,9 @@ obj-$(CONFIG_$(PHASE_)NVME) += nvme/
 obj-$(CONFIG_XEN) += xen/
 obj-$(CONFIG_$(PHASE_)FPGA) += fpga/
 obj-$(CONFIG_$(PHASE_)VIDEO) += video/
+# srgn_splash drives the display with raw register writes, no video uclass --
+# it needs the directory without the rest of CONFIG_VIDEO.
+obj-$(CONFIG_SRGN_SPLASH) += video/
 
 obj-y += bus/
 
diff --git a/drivers/video/Kconfig b/drivers/video/Kconfig
index c2acc131..6e9b1149 100644
--- a/drivers/video/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/video/Kconfig
@@ -1417,4 +1417,15 @@ config SPL_HIDE_LOGO_VERSION
       Enable this option to hide this information.
 endif
 
+config SRGN_SPLASH
+	bool "srgn_splash boot logo command for D1s MIPI-DSI panels"
+	depends on BOARD_SUNXI && RISCV
+	help
+	  Adds the srgn_splash command, which brings up the D1/D1s display
+	  pipeline (DE2 mixer, TCON, DSI host, D-PHY), runs the panel DCS
+	  init sequence out of the control device tree, scans out an
+	  RGB565 framebuffer, and describes it to the kernel as a standard
+	  simple-framebuffer node so simpledrm keeps the logo alive until
+	  the real DRM stack takes over.
+
 endmenu
